---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Sniffr — Pricing">
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="px-6 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-16 md:pb-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold">
        Pricing
      </p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl font-semibold tracking-tight mt-3 text-balance">
        Free until your fourth client pays.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-8 text-lg md:text-xl text-[var(--color-muted)] measure">
        Every tier is the whole product for the dogs in it: walk reports, photos,
        scheduling, payments, and an AI connector for every family. You pay when your
        business grows, and only then.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Tiers -->
  <section class="px-6 pb-24 md:pb-32">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 md:gap-8 items-start">
        <!-- Sniff -->
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl ring-2 ring-[var(--color-accent)] p-6 md:p-7 shadow-[0_20px_60px_-20px_rgba(184,80,30,0.2)]">
          <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
            <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Sniff</h2>
            <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-bg)] border border-[var(--color-rule)] text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold">Start here</span>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-4">
            <span class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold">Free</span>
            <span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]"> to 3 paying clients</span>
          </p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)]">then $29/mo</p>
          <p class="mt-5 text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
            The solo operator's whole toolkit. You walk the dogs; Sniffr runs the rest.
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">✓</span><span>Clients book and pay through the app</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">✓</span><span>Walk reports with photos and voice</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">✓</span><span>Windows and Horizon scheduling</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">✓</span><span>Every dog's record, kept for its family</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">✓</span><span>AI connector for you and your clients</span></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-6 pt-5 border-t border-[var(--color-rule)] text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
            Your first three paying clients are free forever. The paywall is client
            number four. Which is to say: the paywall is your business working.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Fetch -->
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl ring-1 ring-[var(--color-rule)] p-6 md:p-7">
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Fetch</h2>
          <p class="mt-4">
            <span class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold">$59</span>
            <span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">/mo</span>
          </p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)]">$590/yr (two months free)</p>
          <p class="mt-5 text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
            Everything in Sniff, plus the parts that go get the next client. Named for
            what it does.
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">✓</span><span>QR intake: your business card is your intake form</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">✓</span><span>Onboarding pipeline and Meet &amp; Greet tracking</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">✓</span><span>Which card brought which client, tracked</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">✓</span><span>Your brand on reports, booking, and emails <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--color-muted)] border border-[var(--color-rule)] rounded-full px-2 py-0.5 ml-1">soon</span></span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">✓</span><span>Your own domain on your booking page <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--color-muted)] border border-[var(--color-rule)] rounded-full px-2 py-0.5 ml-1">soon</span></span></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-6 pt-5 border-t border-[var(--color-rule)] text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
            Sniff runs the business you have. Fetch brings you the one you're building.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Pack -->
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl ring-1 ring-[var(--color-rule)] p-6 md:p-7">
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Pack</h2>
          <p class="mt-4">
            <span class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold">$99</span>
            <span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">/mo</span>
          </p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)]">+ $15 per active walker</p>
          <p class="mt-5 text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
            Everything in Fetch, for a team. A multi-walker shop is a pack; this tier is
            named for what you built.
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">✓</span><span>Add walkers; Sniffr learns who walks who</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">✓</span><span>Assignment, capacity, and blackout tools</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">✓</span><span>Team scheduling across your whole Horizon</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">✓</span><span>Time off and PTO tracking</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">✓</span><span>Gusto payroll sync <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--color-muted)] border border-[var(--color-rule)] rounded-full px-2 py-0.5 ml-1">soon</span></span></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-6 pt-5 border-t border-[var(--color-rule)] text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
            An active walker is anyone who walked at least once that month. Nobody on the
            bench costs you anything.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Every tier includes -->
      <div class="mt-16 max-w-3xl">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
          Every tier, no asterisks
        </h2>
        <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            <strong>We never take a cut of your revenue.</strong> Card fees are Stripe's
            own rates and we add nothing on top. Your prices, your Stripe account, your
            money. Sniffr's fee is the subscription, full stop.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Your brand on your work.</strong> Walk reports, booking flows, and
            the intake path carry your business's name, on every tier. The app belongs
            to the dog; the work belongs to you.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>AI included, everywhere.</strong> Your clients can connect their own
            AI assistant to their dog's record, and you can run your operation through
            yours. No add-on, no metering, on every tier.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Leave whenever.</strong> Month to month, cancel anytime, and your
            clients come with you. Annual billing is ten months for twelve.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- The comparison that matters -->
      <div class="mt-16 max-w-3xl">
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl ring-1 ring-[var(--color-rule)] p-6 md:p-8">
          <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
            For scale: the marketplace apps keep 20 to 40 cents of every dollar your
            business earns. On a typical solo walker's month, that's more than a thousand
            dollars. Sniffr's biggest tier is $99 and we never touch the transaction.
          </p>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)]">
          And for the families: dog owners never pay Sniffr. The record belongs to the
          dog, free, whoever they hire.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- CTA -->
      <div class="mt-20 max-w-3xl">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance">
          Start with the three clients you can't lose.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed measure">
          Every walker has a few clients who are more friends than customers. Bring them,
          try everything, pay nothing. Setup calls are 30 minutes, run by the founder,
          and your free tier starts the same day.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
          <a
            href="mailto:joseph@papyruslabs.ai?subject=Sniffr%20setup%20call"
            class="bg-[var(--color-ink)] text-[var(--color-bg)] px-6 py-3 rounded-md font-medium hover:bg-[var(--color-accent)] transition-colors"
          >
            Book a setup call
          </a>
          <a
            href="/roadmap"
            class="text-[var(--color-ink)] underline decoration-[var(--color-rule)] underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-[var(--color-accent)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent)] px-2 py-3"
          >
            See the roadmap &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-8 text-xs text-[var(--color-muted)]">
          Prices in USD. Items marked "soon" are in active development; the roadmap has
          dates.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
